      {
        "id": 2317107201,
        "node_id": "PR_kwDOLBN4sM6KHEAB",
        "number": 41,
        "state": "closed",
        "title": "Allow upserting data as vector",
        "body": "I stumbled upon this problem while using the sample code provided in the console. If the index is created with an embedding model, we still try to use `Vector` type with only data field. It should have been `Data`, but I think this is a mistake that can happen a lot. So, we now allow such usages. If this is wrong, server will reject it anyway, just like it does.",
        "html_url": "https://github.com/upstash/vector-py/pull/41",
        "created_at": "2025-02-05T09:23:50Z",
